<%# State label + declined note — VIEWER-AGNOSTIC (no current_user), so it renders
    identically in request and broadcast contexts. accept!/conclude! broadcast this
    to the whole debate stream. The per-viewer accept/decline/conclude affordances
    live in the sibling `_debate_actions` partial. Local: debate. Pinned dom_id so
    the status Turbo-Stream replaces land here.

    The state colour comes from `ds_debate_state_color` (Slice 9 Task 4.5 review) —
    the design system's exported `DEBATE_STATE_COLOR`, shared with the sibling
    `_debate_card`, which used to hold a second inline copy of the same hash. A HELPER
    and not a shared partial precisely because of this file's broadcast path: helpers
    are available to `ApplicationController.render`, and a nested partial rendered
    inside a job is one more thing that can raise where nobody sees it. %>
<% state_color = ds_debate_state_color(debate.status) %>
<span id="<%= dom_id(debate, :status) %>" class="debate-status flex flex-col min-w-0">
  <span class="debate-state text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-<%= state_color %>"><%= debate.status.titleize %></span>
  <%# ACTIVE ONLY. A round counter is an in-progress affordance: on a concluded debate
      Debate#current_round has already run one past rounds_limit (turns.count / 2 + 1),
      and current_phase is nil by design — while a debate concluded EARLY would read
      "Round 2 of 4" under a "Concluded" label, which describes a debate still waiting
      for two more rounds that will never come. The state label alone is the truth there.
      This is why current_round is printed RAW: while active, post_turn has not yet
      capped, so turns.count <= 2*rounds_limit - 1 and current_round <= rounds_limit
      already. A [current_round, rounds_limit].min here would be a guard that can never
      fire, whose only justification is the overshoot the `active?` test above excludes —
      so it would read as protection this line does not have. The invariant lives in the
      guard; do not print this outside it. %>
  <% if debate.active? %>
    <span class="debate-round text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-grey">
      Round <%= debate.current_round %> of <%= debate.rounds_limit %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
  <% if debate.declined? %>
    <span class="text-sm text-grey">@<%= debate.opponent.username %> declined the challenge.</span>
  <% end %>
</span>
